  "question": {
    "text": "At constant temperature, a gas is at a pressure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>940</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hg</mi></math>. The pressure at which its volume decreases by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math> is ______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hg</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1567",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>From&nbsp;Boyle&#39;s Law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>940</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;mm of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Hg</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Pressure at which volume is reduced by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Volume decreased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Then,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>940</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1567</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>1567</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hg</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
